{"abstract":"Prediction has a long history in the social sciences, and advances in comput-ing and statistics have transformed our ability to predict in a wide range of domains.However, concerns have been raised about an indiscriminate application of a predic-tive logic, and crime is an area where this is quite pronounced. Indeed, while the po-lice, correctional service, and criminal courts have become increasingly reliant on dig-ital systems of prediction, critics have drawn our attention to numerous issues andcomplexities attendant to this process. This chapter looks at prediction in the crimino-logical realm and provides an overview of key arguments concerning the way data aregenerated, organized, and used as input for predictive tools and technologies, and howthe results are interpreted in the context of criminal justice. By doing so, it aims toshow that the discussions surrounding prediction highlight how digital tools are trans-forming the nature of knowledge and expertise within the criminal justice system","author_count":5,"contributors":["Galis, Vasilis","Oppen Ingebrigtsen Gundhus, Helen","Kilis, Emil"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-798545"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Oslo"],"keyword":["Criminal justice system","Prediction","Predictive policing","Risk Assessment"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"prediction","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1515/9783111062037-043","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-798545","ids":["itu-889d153b-5327-4994-829b-3c9e6d663a4d"],"keyword":["Prediction","criminal justice system","predictive policing","risk assessment"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-0FC0CC39DDFB4F8FC4B1C5DDDB8D4402"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1515/9783111062037-043","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Welfare","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"no","key":"university of oslo","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Oslo","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vasilis","key":"galispau","last":"Galis","locid":"443362d7-b255-460d-a559-0fa80a8d9fbc","name":"Galis, Vasilis","orcid":"0000-0002-4621-3699","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Helen","key":"oppeningebrigtsengundhuspau","last":"Oppen Ingebrigtsen Gundhus","name":"Oppen Ingebrigtsen Gundhus, Helen","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Emil","key":"kilispau","last":"Kilis","name":"Kilis, Emil","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Mareile","key":"kaufmannpedh","last":"Kaufmann","name":"Kaufmann, Mareile","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Heidi Mork","key":"lomellpedh","last":"Lomell","name":"Lomell, Heidi Mork","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1515/9783111062037-043","eisbn":["9783111062037"],"isbn":["9783111061931"],"issn":["27479269"],"pages":"371-379","publisher":"De Gruyter","series":"De Gruyter Contemporary Social Sciences Handbooks","status":"p","title":"De Gruyter Handbook of Digital Criminology","volume":"6"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-889d153b-5327-4994-829b-3c9e6d663a4d"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Prediction","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-798545","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"This chapter interrogates the question of what defines predictive policing. Our point of departure is notions in Science and Technology Studies that attend to how boundary objects such as predictive policing are produced through the interrelation of politics, sociotechnical imaginaries, and contestations. Through ethnographic inquiry on the empirical case of the POL-INTEL platform of the Danish police, we follow the evolution and demarcations in the (re)-classifications of POL-INTEL from predictive to non-predictive. In so doing, we situate POL-INTEL in the wider international context regarding the development of predictive policing and investigate the boundary work between predictive policing and similar concepts such as Intelligence-Led Policing. Concisely, we argue that the development of the notion of predictive policing is fundamentally unstable and tied to political and economic interests.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Karlsson, Björn","Galis, Vasilis"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-828160"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Big data","Critical criminology","Digital policing","Law enforcement","Predictive policing","Surveillance technology"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"what constitutes predictive policing the case of pol intel in denmark","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4337/9781035323036","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-828160","ids":["itu-7ab4c71c-5a57-4d63-99e4-03f1c7eba8ea"],"keyword":["Big Data","Critical Criminology","Digital Policing","Law Enforcement","Predictive Policing","Surveillance Technology","rime Forecasting"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-4-5-AA0BB3B63F55270DAFE021F87B9FD968"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4337/9781035323036","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4337/9781035323036.00012","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies of Social Order"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Björn","key":"karlssonpau","last":"Karlsson","locid":"3d49de50-0620-46fe-ae15-53b12dfb8649","name":"Karlsson, Björn","orcid":"0009-0006-0393-3676","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vasilis","key":"galispau","last":"Galis","locid":"443362d7-b255-460d-a559-0fa80a8d9fbc","name":"Galis, Vasilis","orcid":"0000-0002-4621-3699","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Vasilis","key":"galispedh","last":"Galis","name":"Galis, Vasilis","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Helene O.I.","key":"gundhuspedh","last":"Gundhus","name":"Gundhus, Helene O.I.","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Antonis","key":"vradispedh","last":"Vradis","name":"Vradis, Antonis","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.4337/9781035323036","eisbn":["9781035323036"],"isbn":["9781035323029"],"pages":"130-155","publisher":"Edward Elgar Publishing","status":"p","title":"Critical Perspectives on Predictive Policing"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","sco