{"abstract":"Based on the empirical case of the POL-INTEL platform used by the Danish police, which is a customized version of Palantir Technologies’ Gotham platform, this article traces the interrelation between scientification and policing in the digital era as articulated in and through a private actor. Ethnographic fieldwork, interviews, publicly available policy documents as well as documents detailing police practices, organization, ambitions and workflows are used to problematize digital policing platforms and practices in terms of wider criminological theories and models. We show that POL-INTEL epitomizes a historical trajectory of scientification through privatization by drawing together intelligence practices, market logics, and datafication methodologies. With this point of departure, we trace back how the entanglement of private actors and the police organization raises concerns about the black boxing of criminological procedures, and the delegation of decisions and knowledge within the criminal justice system to private actors lacking public values.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Galis, Vasilis","Karlsson, Björn"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-818228"],"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Predictive policing","Privatization","Science and Technology Studies","scientification"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"scientification through privatization pol intel in denmark","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-818228","identifier":[{"id":"105010124561","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-011e4cae-aac1-4750-b1ff-27d6c17c0eb5"],"keyword":["intelligence-led policing","predictive policing","privatization","science and technology studies","scientification"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-6E21F4DC23548A326FDC24BF45DC6A47"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Welfare","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies of Social Order"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vasilis","key":"galispau","last":"Galis","locid":"443362d7-b255-460d-a559-0fa80a8d9fbc","name":"Galis, Vasilis","orcid":"0000-0002-4621-3699","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Björn","key":"karlssonpau","last":"Karlsson","locid":"3d49de50-0620-46fe-ae15-53b12dfb8649","name":"Karlsson, Björn","orcid":"0009-0006-0393-3676","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"X"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Undefined"]},"sid":["itu-011e4cae-aac1-4750-b1ff-27d6c17c0eb5"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Scientification through privatization : POL-INTEL in Denmark","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-818228","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"This insightful book investigates the growing use of digital technologies to support welfare provision and examines which digital tools can have the greatest impact. It explores how these technologies influence and are influenced by social and cultural relations, working life, education, healthcare, markets, and organizations. Vasilis Galis and Vasileios-Spyridon Vlassis bring together renowned experts who analyze digital technologies for welfare provision as sociotechnical phenomena, that is, the welfare state is mutually constructed by welfare practices and digital technologies, an outcome of organizational reconfiguration, political–economic visions, and socio-technical imaginaries. They demonstrate that digitalization is not simply a question of implementing digital technologies but also an introduction of new governmental ideas that transform both the public sector and its services as well as inter-state and state-society relations. The book explores how the rapid implementation of digital tools in the provision of welfare services is bringing fundamental changes to welfare and provides experienced-based accounts of the transformations occurring in public service work. Digitalization, Data and Welfare is an essential resource for students and academics in welfare studies. Its practical insights into inter-state and state-society relations will also greatly benefit welfare policymakers and practitioners in innovation, science and technology.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Galis, Vasilis","Vlassis, Vasilieos-Spyridon"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-828146"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Data","Digitalisation","Governance","Welfare","Welfare state"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"digitalization data and welfare sociotechnical approaches to service delivery","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"db","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"rem","url":"https://doi.org/10.4337/9781035338153","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-828146","ids":["itu-3993639c-82aa-442c-b94f-e8c8f80263e6"],"keyword":["Digitalisation","Governance","Social Provision","Welfare","Welfare State","data"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-29F7C15939EE046E56BAD96D5B076699"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"rem","url":"https://doi.org/10.4337/9781035338153","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Welfare","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies of Social Order"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vasilis","key":"galispau","last":"Galis","locid":"443362d7-b255-460d-a559-0fa80a8d9fbc","name":"Galis, Vasilis","orcid":"0000-0002-4621-3699","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vasilieos-Spyridon","key":"vlassispau","last":"Vlassis","locid":"0537edb0-1a18-425e-8a82-c92b2882a597","name":"Vlassis, Vasilieos-Spyridon","orcid":"0000-0002-4098-9015","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9781035338153"],"isbn":["9781035338146"],"pages":"268","publisher":"Edward Elgar Publishing","series":"Sociology, Social Policy and Education","status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-3993639c-82aa-442c-b94f-e8c8f80263e6"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Digitalization, Data and Welfare : Sociotechnical Approaches to Service Delivery","type":"Book","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-828146","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"As Western countries have deepened their levels of digitalisation of the public sector, governments have become increasingly interested in abandoning, or at least loosening, some of the more rigid bureaucratic structures governing the state apparatus and experimenting with the agile methodologies that grew out of Silicon Valley around the turn of the millennium. In this chapter, we argue that this increasingly widespread agile public digitalisation style is creating a need to pay more attention to the development and design, delivery, efficiency, and governance of digital public services, the infrastructures they rely on, and the societal impact of this so-called agile transformation. We suggest understanding this problem through the prism of response-ability, an empirically derived concept consisting of three distinct but overlapping dimensions regarding the ability of the state to (a) respond fast and flexibly, (b) be held accountable for its decisions, and (c) be responsive to citizens and stakeholders. These three dimensions have always been central to democratic statehood but are re-actualised and gain new meaning as they become part of the processes of public digitalisation and agile transformation. The chapter consists of four sections, each presenting a theme within agile and digital public transformation, in relation to which the concept of response-ability comes into play. The themes are governance, insourcing, legacy and maintenance, and citizen involvement. The sections draw on the authors’ knowledge and empirical studies of the public sectors in the Nordic countries and the UK, and draw on various data types, from interviews with key actors to field visits and publicly available documents, as well as, for some of us, previous industry experience.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Papazu, Irina","Wang, Cancan","Perriam, Jessamy","Marttila, Sanna-Maria"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-828176"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Agile development","Agile transformation","Citizen involvement","Digital transformation","Governance","Insourcing","Outsourcing","Response ability"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"outsourcing response ability tales from agile governance","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4337/9781035338153.00013","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-828176","ids":["itu-c6e8396d-fa41-45f7-a68d-b47e64be0722"],"keyword":["Agile Development","Agile transformation","Citizen involvement","Digital transformation","Governance","Insourcing","Legacy technology","Outsourcing","Response-ability"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-C3B2E4A79BC8A1BFE556580F8C9B3ACD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4337/9781035338153.00013","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Climate IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Welfare","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Irina","key":"papazupau","last":"Papazu","locid":"6ec63914-1f4e-4708-8830-1b054c2ee03a","name":"Papazu, Irina","orcid":"0000-0002-4178-3676","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Cancan","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","locid":"605b59ab-91b4-4f8e-bb12-df68ce0491c5","name":"Wang, Cancan","orcid":"0000-0002-9065-6884","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jessamy","key":"perriampau","last":"Perriam","locid":"4ca57c3b-1d1f-4ecf-87b0-fe690510c887","name":"Perriam, Jessamy","orcid":"0000-0002-6362-8634","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sanna-Maria","key":"marttilapau","last":"Marttila","locid":"528393a3-e784-47a8-85be-c81d44c393bd","name":"Marttila, Sanna-Maria","orcid":"0000-0003-3793-5021","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Vasilis","key":"galispedh","last":"Galis","name":"Galis, Vasilis","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Vasileios-Spyridon","key":"vlassispedh","last":"Vlassis","name":"Vlassis, Vasileios-Spyridon","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.4337/9781035338153.00013","eisbn":["9781035338153"],"isbn":["9781035338146"],"pages":"74-91","publisher":"Edward Elgar Publishing","status":"p","title":"Digitalization, Data and Welfare"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-c6e8396d-fa41-45f7-a68d-b47e64be0722"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Outsourcing response-ability : Tales from ‘agile’ governance","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-828176","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"When Palantir Technologies customized the Gotham platform into POL-INTEL, a data integration and analysis platform purchased and used by the Danish police, it also enforced a new ontology that simultaneously shaped the police organization and policing practices. In this context, the concept of ontology should be understood in a twofold, albeit interconnected, way: it stands for its usual philosophical burden, but also refers to a centralized concept repository. In Computer Science, ontology refers to the basic concepts for how data is structured. Based on a series of interviews with Palantir engineers and police-officer users of POL-INTEL, this paper investigates what kind of politics, concepts, and bias in the form of data are inserted, processed and materialized in and by POL-INTEL’s ontology. We argue that POL-INTEL’s ontology is inherently political, as it is articulated by an assemblage of data, ideological positions, and economic concerns that are translated into the Danish context. POL-INTEL as a vector of platformization of police work also implies ideological choices with important consequences for the organizational life and accountability of law enforcement, establishing new distributions of skills between the platform and police officers.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Galis, Vasilis","Karlsson, Björn"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-764502"],"filters":{"added":"2024-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Ontological politics","Ontology","Palantir","Predictive policing"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a world of palantir ontological politics in the danish police s pol intel","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/1369118X.2024.2410255","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-764502","identifier":[{"id":"85205286090","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-162d4df5-ad7b-415a-ad30-3fb1bcd9ca8c"],"keyword":["Ontological politics","Ontology","Palantir","Predictive policing"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-29BA85ABDA6F6FA69A77125F7AB59F2F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/1369118X.2024.2410255","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Welfare","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vasilis","key":"galispau","last":"Galis","locid":"443362d7-b255-460d-a559-0fa80a8d9fbc","name":"Galis, Vasilis","orcid":"0000-0002-4621-3699","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Björn","key":"karlssonpau","last":"Karlsson","locid":"3d49de50-0620-46fe-ae15-53b12dfb8649","name":"Karlsson, Björn","orcid":"0009-0006-0393-3676","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/1369118x.2024.2410255","issn":["1369118X","14684462"],"issn_org":["1369118X"],"journal":"Information, Communication & Society","pages":"1-19","publisher":"Taylor & Francis","status":"p","title":"Information, Communication & Society"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85205286090"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-162d4df5-ad7b-415a-ad30-3fb1bcd9ca8c"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A world of Palantir : Ontological politics in the Danish police’s POL-INTEL","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-764502","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"The integration of automated decision-making systems has transformed police work and our understanding of security and surveillance. Despite a growing theoretical literature on shifts in policing due to widespread analytical platform adoption, the public's understanding and perception of these changes are largely unexplored. This study aims to bridge this gap by empirically examining citizens’ perspectives on the new dynamics of police work in two societies with varying levels of experience with automation in the public sector: Estonia and Sweden. By combining data from a representative, scenario-based quantitative survey conducted among the general population (n = 2500) and qualitative storytelling techniques implemented in classroom settings with students (n = 23) who take classes with a focus on critical data studies, this research seeks to investigate people’s imaginaries, concerns, and expectations regarding predictive policing. The findings shed light on the observation that, in the era of data, the police are not solely perceived as an institution ensuring security or as a source of citizen apprehension related to surveillance. Rather, the transformations in police work are understood as ‘distant technologies’, wherein individuals, be they, citizens, or police officers, are increasingly removed from the direct application of these technologies. This article uncovers that when citizens possess low levels of trust in the police, the implementation of automation can further exacerbate the disconnect between citizens and the state. Furthermore, this research proposes an innovative approach to studying automated systems by combining scenario-based and storytelling methods, thereby making a valuable contribution to methodologies employed in the study of data.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Galis, Vasilis","Masso, Anu","Kasapoglu, Tayfun","Kaun, Anne"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-730188"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Estonia","Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Södertörn University","Tallinn University of Technology"],"keyword":["Data","Datafication","Platform","Predictive policing","Storytelling","Survey"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"citizens perspectives on platformisation of police work a scenario and story based exploration in estonia and sweden","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/1369118X.2024.2333842","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-730188","identifier":[{"id":"85189619851","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-afe9ae19-f59a-4fbb-859f-40596a4d4a17"],"keyword":["Data","Datafication","Platform","Predictive policing","Storytelling","Survey"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-374DA48B76B22F995FADCA346F62DEFB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/1369118X.2024.2333842","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Welfare","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"ee","key":"tallinn university of technology","loc":["Estonia","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Tallinn University of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"se","key":"södertörn university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Södertörn University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vasilis","key":"galispau","last":"Galis","locid":"443362d7-b255-460d-a559-0fa80a8d9fbc","name":"Galis, Vasilis","orcid":"0000-0002-4621-3699","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Anu","key":"massopau","last":"Masso","name":"Masso, Anu","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Tayfun","key":"kasapoglupau","last":"Kasapoglu","name":"Kasapoglu, Tayfun","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne","key":"kaunpau","last":"Kaun","name":"Kaun, Anne","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/1369118x.2024.2333842","issn":["1369118X","14684462"],"issn_org":["1369118X"],"journal":"Information, Communication & Society","publisher":"Taylor & Francis","status":"p","title":"Information, Communication & Society"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85189619851"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-afe9ae19-f59a-4fbb-859f-40596a4d4a17"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Citizens’ perspectives on platformisation of police work : a scenario and story-based exploration in Estonia and Sweden","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-730188","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Data integration and analytics platforms promise the ‘desilosation’ of databases by connecting heterogeneous data from different databases. In this chapter, we introduce platforms as a timely Big Data fuelled tool of policing, by comparatively discussing empirical insights from platform projects in Denmark, Germany, and Norway, all with reference to the market leader Palantir Technologies. We ask: What motivates police organizations to use these platforms and what kind of transformations come along with the implementation of data analysis platforms? We conclude by arguing that despite challenges and conflicts with Palantir in Germany and Norway, data analysis and integration platforms have the potential to reconfigure work practices and employment conditions, ultimately challenging the long-standing professional culture of regulating the police work environments.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Galis, Vasilis","Egbert, Simon","Oppen Ingebrigtsen Gundhus, Helen","Thea Wathne, Christin"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-776410"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Germany","Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Bielefeld University","Oslo Metropolitan University","University of Oslo"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the platformization of policing a cross national analysis","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-776410","ids":["itu-6b32541b-ad05-46b1-853c-de8a6a210f2d"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-9E00D8C4C2523FBE6E9D05BBA6F42F70"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Welfare","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"bielefeld university","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Bielefeld University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"no","key":"university of oslo","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Oslo","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"no","key":"oslo metropolitan university","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Oslo Metropolitan University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vasilis","key":"galispau","last":"Galis","locid":"443362d7-b255-460d-a559-0fa80a8d9fbc","name":"Galis, Vasilis","orcid":"0000-0002-4621-3699","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Simon","key":"egbertpau","last":"Egbert","name":"Egbert, Simon","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Helen","key":"oppeningebrigtsengundhuspau","last":"Oppen Ingebrigtsen Gundhus","name":"Oppen Ingebrigtsen Gundhus, Helen","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Christin","key":"theawathnepau","last":"Thea Wathne","name":"Thea Wathne, Christin","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Tereza","key":"østbøkuldovapedh","last":"Østbø Kuldova","name":"Østbø Kuldova, Tereza","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Helene","key":"oppeningebrigtsengundhuspedh","last":"Oppen Ingebrigtsen Gundhus","name":"Oppen Ingebrigtsen Gundhus, Helene","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Christin","key":"theawathnepedh","last":"Thea Wathne","name":"Thea Wathne, Christin","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-031-68326-8_11","eisbn":["9783031683268"],"isbn":["9783031683251"],"issn":["27305368"],"pages":"349-392","publisher":"Palgrave Macmillan","series":"Palgrave's Critical Policing Studies","status":"p","title":"Policing and Intelligence in the Global Big Data Era","volume":"I"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-6b32541b-ad05-46b1-853c-de8a6a210f2d"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Platformization of Policing : A Cross-National Analysis","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-776410","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"This article problematises the invocation of the stepping stone hypothesis for platform labour by Danish policymakers, namely the argument that digital labour platforms facilitate transitioning to typical employment, especially for groups of vulnerable workers. Tracing the origins of the stepping stone hypothesis back to the international literature on temporary work agencies and workfare policies triggered by neoliberal policy shifts, the article explores the ideological underpinning of the hypothesis in the Danish context, as Danish policymakers invoked it without possessing relevant data. This article questions the stepping stone narrative drawing on policy document analysis and expert interviews, but also on interviews with platform housecleaners, whose backgrounds, experiences, and aspirations indicate that they do not perceive platform labour as a stepping stone. Early Danish research on platform labour has not been premised on the workers’ perspectives. We claim that policymakers’ positive depiction of platform labour serves towards social and institutional stabilisation of technoprecarious – migrant – labour as a desired and inescapable future of work within the Danish labour market.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Galis, Vasilis","Floros, Konstantinos"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-776418"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Denmark","Gig workers","Policymaking","Stepping stone","migrant labour","platform labour"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"platform labour as a stepping stone challenging the dominant narrative for danish housecleaning platforms","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-776418","identifier":[{"id":"85211124678","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-7ca83646-d8a7-438b-bf3b-066d4df3e648"],"keyword":["Denmark","gig workers","migrant labour","platform labour","policymaking","stepping stone","technoprecarity;"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-D3A0F386154CCA19481D1E363C939703"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Welfare","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vasilis","key":"galispau","last":"Galis","locid":"443362d7-b255-460d-a559-0fa80a8d9fbc","name":"Galis, Vasilis","orcid":"0000-0002-4621-3699","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Konstantinos","key":"florospau","last":"Floros","locid":"20ad2ae0-df32-484d-84ed-f65810600cfa","name":"Floros, Konstantinos","orcid":"0009-0002-4687-796X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"X"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Undefined"]},"sid":["itu-7ca83646-d8a7-438b-bf3b-066d4df3e648"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Platform Labour as a Stepping Stone? : Challenging the Dominant Narrative for Danish Housecleaning Platforms","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-776418","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"This introduction to the special issue on data integration and analytics platforms provides an overview of the current importance of these platforms, with particular reference to the market leader, Palantir Technologies. In addition to the platformization of many areas of society through the use of data integration and analytics platforms, we argue that, where Palantir platforms are used, the process of ‘Palantirization’ can also be observed, because Palantir as a company is characterized not only by powerful platforms, but also by particular market entry techniques and, in particular, a decidedly political stance. This, we argue, is part of the package when Palantir's platforms were adopted.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Galis, Vasilis","Egbert, Simon","Oppen Ingebrigtsen Gundhus, Helen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-776430"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Germany","Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Bielefeld University","University of Oslo"],"keyword":["AI","Data analysis","Data integration","Palantir","Platforms"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the role of data integration and analysis platforms in contemporary society an introduction","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85211135299","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-776430","identifier":[{"id":"85211135299","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-9e13c780-44ec-46f6-8194-9e3bdf28094f"],"keyword":["AI","Palantir","data analysis","data integration","platforms"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-389B13227F16A4DBF9543E774186183C"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Welfare","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"bielefeld university","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Bielefeld University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"no","key":"university of oslo","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Oslo","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vasilis","key":"galispau","last":"Galis","locid":"443362d7-b255-460d-a559-0fa80a8d9fbc","name":"Galis, Vasilis","orcid":"0000-0002-4621-3699","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Simon","key":"egbertpau","last":"Egbert","name":"Egbert, Simon","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Helen","key":"oppeningebrigtsengundhuspau","last":"Oppen Ingebrigtsen Gundhus","name":"Oppen Ingebrigtsen Gundhus, Helen","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/1369118x.2024.2433556","issn":["1369118X","14684462"],"issn_org":["1369118X"],"journal":"Information, Communication & Society","pages":"1","publisher":"Taylor & Francis","status":"p","title":"Information, Communication & Society"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85211135299"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-9e13c780-44ec-46f6-8194-9e3bdf28094f"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The role of data integration and analysis platforms in contemporary society : an introduction","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-776430","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"author_count":2,"contributors":["Galis, Vasilis","Pedersen, Anja Møller"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-719874"],"filters":{"added":"2024-03","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"pop","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"pol intel lad os tale om de menneskeretlige konsekvenser og demokratiske konsekvenser af datadrevet politi","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"djc","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-719874","ids":["ku-3970ac01-b71b-4fe5-8a6b-fa8208b4832f"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-702498228BDFE93124D66B80AF995999"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Law, Area of Research, Centre for Information and Innovation Law"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Vasilis","key":"galispau","last":"Galis","name":"Galis, Vasilis","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","first":"Anja Møller","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"57bc53a9-ba10-4efa-bf03-a027c58eb990","name":"Pedersen, Anja Møller","orcid":"0000-0002-5490-4895","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"journal":"Radar","status":"p","title":"Radar"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-3970ac01-b71b-4fe5-8a6b-fa8208b4832f"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"POL-INTEL: Lad os tale om de menneskeretlige konsekvenser og demokratiske konsekvenser af datadrevet politi","type":"Journal Comment","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-719874","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"This introduction together with the whole special issue on border technologies challenges the limitations of potentially simplistic understandings of contestation, disputes, and political intervention inherent in many accounts of material politics. How do border technologies turn borders into a contested space and how do they come to matter for specific affected communities, especially migrants? How do border technologies manifest hegemonic border-control regimes and thereby marginalise their contestations? Or else, how do they open up alternative versions of the border? Simplified notions of material publics assume that controversial issues may easily turn public. They are also too narrowly framed within the logics of the nation state, de jure citizenship, and specific political articulations of contestation as legitimate within representative democracies. Therefore, these notions disregard opaque, non-transparent forms of government as they are in place through border control regimes, on the one hand, and other less visible forms of contestation deriving from migrant issues and struggles as non-citizens, on the other hand. Migrants concerned with these issues are already marginalised population groups in the context of border technologies. They potentially struggle to make public issues of concern among a wider audience. The introduction together with the special issue expands the analytical repertoire, first, to understand forms of (im)possibilities of contestations related to border technologies and how they are co-shaped by socio-material and epistemic conditions; and second, to include less visible types of material politics, as contesting articulations may appear differently and remain only partially known to wider publics.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Galis, Vasilis","Amelung, Nina"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-683623"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Portugal"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Lisbon"],"keyword":["Border technologies","Contestation","Material politics","in visibility","migrant subjects","political articulations"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"border control technologies introduction","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/09505431.2023.2234932","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-683623","identifier":[{"id":"85165701519","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-3ececbc4-fb00-47f6-a0d7-da56df56c593"],"keyword":["(in)visibility","Border technologies","contestation","material politics","migrant subjects","political articulations"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-414E0E7581D6562B404BED55EDD995E9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/epdf/10.1080/09505431.2023.2234932?needAccess=true&role=button","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/09505431.2023.2234932","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Welfare","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"pt","key":"university of lisbon","loc":["Portugal","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Lisbon","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vasilis","key":"galispau","last":"Galis","locid":"443362d7-b255-460d-a559-0fa80a8d9fbc","name":"Galis, Vasilis","orcid":"0000-0002-4621-3699","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Nina","key":"amelungpau","last":"Amelung","name":"Amelung, Nina","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/09505431.2023.2234932","issn":["09505431","14701189"],"issn_org":["09505431"],"journal":"Science as Culture","publisher":"Routledge","status":"p","title":"Science as Culture"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85165701519"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-3ececbc4-fb00-47f6-a0d7-da56df56c593"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Border control technologies : introduction","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-683623","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Digital connectivity of queer migrants on the move to Europe plays a crucial role in confronting border regimes, heteronormativity and racist oppression. ICTs at the disposal of queer migrants interrupt the material politics of silence and violence. However, digital technology also implies serious hazards. Queer migrants use digital space to empower themselves, to build networks, and to trace, reach and create safer spaces of care. This paper conceptualises how care is materialised in self-organised actions and horizontal relationships that question power regimes and commodification practices while introducing the notion of radical digital care. Digital spaces of (radical) care constitute safe spaces of compassion where people can be heard and believed. They act as points of reference for queer people seeking recognition and care. Moreover, queer migration constitutes constant shifting between subject and care positions that redefine the notion of home and safety and the material ordering of migration itself. Based on a qualitative study of ten semi-structured interviews with solidarians and migrants, this paper reveals how the appropriation of digital media by queer migrants re-arranges the material politics of the borderland by contesting border technologies, and through radical care, allows communities to live through hardship, fear, and abuse.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Galis, Vasilis","Makrygianni, Vasiliki"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-683625"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Greece"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Aristotle University of Thessaloniki"],"keyword":["Queer migration","autonomy of migration","radical digital space"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"practices of radical digital care towards autonomous queer migration","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/09505431.2023.2221292","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-683625","identifier":[{"id":"85161668669","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-f8d428b3-e6f0-45b5-86be-09f74fb5c390"],"keyword":["Queer migration","autonomy of migration","radical digital space"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3C994B0CDD9B4DFC1411AC527BBEA82C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/epdf/10.1080/09505431.2023.2221292?needAccess=true&role=button","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/09505431.2023.2221292","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.academia.edu/attachments/103575833/download_file?st=MTczODI0MDM3OCwxMzAuMjI2LjEzMi4xMA%3D%3D&s=profile","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Welfare","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gr","key":"aristotle university of thessaloniki","loc":["Greece","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Aristotle University of Thessaloniki","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vasilis","key":"galispau","last":"Galis","locid":"443362d7-b255-460d-a559-0fa80a8d9fbc","name":"Galis, Vasilis","orcid":"0000-0002-4621-3699","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Vasiliki","key":"makrygiannipau","last":"Makrygianni","name":"Makrygianni, Vasiliki","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/09505431.2023.2221292","issn":["09505431","14701189"],"issn_org":["09505431"],"issue":"3","journal":"Science as Culture","pages":"387-410","publisher":"Routledge","status":"p","title":"Science as Culture","volume":"32"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85161668669"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-f8d428b3-e6f0-45b5-86be-09f74fb5c390"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Practices of radical digital care : Towards autonomous queer migration","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-683625","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"The Migration Mobile offers an account of the very different technologies implicated in border crossing and migration management. Borders have been sites of contestations and struggles over who belongs and who does not, who is and is not allowed to move freely in transnational or national spaces. Embedded as they are in the bordering process, policing and security practices produce the irregularity and illegitimacy of the migrating subject. At the same time, border practices simultaneously imply processes of dissidence and resistance. Border infrastructures and resistance to bordering practices refer to dynamic and complex interactions between migrants and non-human others, technologies at the borderland and elsewhere. Border guards, EU officials, Frontex officers, activists, NGOs and solidarity networks configure both hybrid alliances of humans/nonhumans and new virtual and urban spaces in order to enforce or resist bordering. Through analyses of empirical cases drawing from the European border regimes the book investigates how technologies employed by states and EU border agencies configure the border regimes; how spaces of migration are configured through uses and re-uses of high-tech technologies; and finally on how the border regimes and ‘the border industrial complex’ are contested reconfigured by the use of ICT by migrants and solidarity networks.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Jørgensen, Martin Bak","Galis, Vasilis"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-115073"],"filters":{"added":"2022-09","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the migration mobile border dissidence sociotechnical resistance and the construction of irregularized migrants","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://rowman.com/ISBN/9781538165164/The-Migration-Mobile-Border-Dissidence-Sociotechnical-Resistance-and-the-Construction-of-Irregularized-Migrants","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-115073","ids":["aau-dfa6187c-38e3-491d-b375-682681875178"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-A0B89DCDE0FFFFDC30B6107C87F88E83"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Culture and Learning","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Culture and Learning, Democracy, Migration and Society (DEMOS)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Politics and Society, MIX - Center for Displacement, Migration and Integration"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Martin Bak","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"5e41f079-bbd2-4a57-a1d3-8fad8c9233de","name":"Jørgensen, Martin Bak","orcid":"0000-0003-0104-8543","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Vasilis","key":"galispau","last":"Galis","name":"Galis, Vasilis","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9781538165171"],"isbn":["9781538165164"],"pages":"3-25","publisher":"Rowman & Littlefield Publishers","series":"Challenging Migration Studies","status":"p","subtitle":"Border Dissidence, Sociotechnical Resistance, and the Construction of Irregularized Migrants","title":"The Migration Mobile"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-dfa6187c-38e3-491d-b375-682681875178"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"The Migration Mobile : Border Dissidence, Sociotechnical Resistance and the Construction of Irregularized Migrants","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-115073","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
